# Citation metadata (https://citation-file-format.github.io/). GitHub reads
# this file for its "Cite this repository" button; Zenodo reads it when a
# release is archived. Keep `version` in step with package.json.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use STAC Lens in your work, please cite it as below.'
type: software
title: 'STAC Lens'
abstract: >-
  A free, open-source, browser-only viewer and health checker for STAC
  (SpatioTemporal Asset Catalog) catalogs and APIs. It draws a catalog's
  structure as a tree with its coverage in time and space alongside, marks
  where the metadata contradicts itself or the specification, and reports
  the difference between what a STAC API declares and what it does when
  asked.
authors:
  - name: 'lavalse'
    alias: 'lavalse'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/rednotfound/stac-lens'
url: 'https://staclens.com'
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-18
keywords:
  - STAC
  - SpatioTemporal Asset Catalog
  - STAC API
  - geospatial
  - Earth observation
  - remote sensing
  - open data
  - GIS
  - metadata quality
  - data visualization
